flowchart TB
accTitle: Perception and grounding action boundary
accDescr: Read and write actions both pass through ActionDispatcher type and capability/resource checks. Write actions additionally use idempotency handling, a handler precondition for expected snapshot version, and the simulator-world port. A workflow-level human approval, where required, is checked separately from dispatcher capability authorization.
    Agent[Agent decision procedure]
    subgraph ReadPath[Read-only perception path]
      ReadRequest[Read request]
      ReadDispatch[ActionDispatcher: type and capability/resource checks]
      Perception[Perception action handler]
      ReadPort[Perception port]
      Snapshot[Current simulated snapshot]
      Observation[Observation with provenance and source version]
      ReadRequest --> ReadDispatch --> Perception --> ReadPort --> Snapshot --> Observation
    end
    subgraph WritePath[State-changing grounding path]
      WriteRequest[Typed write request]
      Approval[Check application-level approval when required]
      WriteDispatch[ActionDispatcher: type and capability/resource checks]
      Idempotency[Inspect prior operation by required key and fingerprint]
      Handler[Grounding action handler precondition: expected snapshot version]
      Claim[Acquire idempotency claim when required]
      Command[Typed simulation command]
      World[SupplyChainSimulationWorld port and adapter]
      Transition[Simulated-world transition]
      WriteRequest --> Approval --> WriteDispatch --> Idempotency --> Handler --> Claim --> Command --> World --> Transition
    end
    Agent --> ReadRequest
    Observation --> Agent
    Agent --> WriteRequest
    Transition --> Agent
